Subject: [BACKPORT->v0.5.13@28b095c] DSV4 non-paged indexer for large prefill chunks (upstream #29619 + #30140), OPT-IN (rev2)

Upstream: a6ee64d23 "[DeepSeek-V4] Add an opt-in non-paged indexer for
long-context prefill (#29619)" + 583e19d22 "Enable non-paged indexer by
default for large prefill chunks (#30140)" (cherry-pick #30436).

KEPT OPT-IN on our pin: SGLANG_OPT_DSV4_NONPAGED_INDEXER defaults to False
here even though upstream #30140 defaulted it to True. Production flips it
only after GPU validation. The #30140 large-chunk threshold
(SGLANG_OPT_DSV4_NONPAGED_INDEXER_MIN_QUERY_TOKENS=8192, per-rank local query
rows) is included.

rev2 (post-review): the pin DOES have prefill CUDA graphs
(init_forward_metadata_prefill already takes use_prefill_cuda_graph and
builds graph compressor plans), so this revision (a) patches
deepseek_v4_backend.py to propagate use_prefill_cuda_graph through
init_forward_metadata_indexer into PagedIndexerMetadata (upstream's own
backend hunk, re-anchored), and (b) restores both upstream graph-context
guards using their PIN-equivalent homes:
  compilation.piecewise_context_manager.is_in_piecewise_cuda_graph
  model_executor.breakable_cuda_graph.context.is_in_breakable_cuda_graph
These are required, not optional: piecewise graph warmup runs a real bs=1
EXTEND batch BEFORE stream capture, so is_current_stream_capturing() alone
would not reject it. As upstream, the normal-decode / target-verify /
raw-decode / CP-resplit callers of init_forward_metadata_indexer keep the
default (False); they are rejected by the ForwardMode.EXTEND and cp_size==1
eligibility checks.

Adaptations vs upstream commits:
- forward_batch._original_forward_mode accessed via getattr: on the pin it is
  a setattr-only attribute (set when a decode batch is rewritten to EXTEND
  under DP max-len padding — exactly our dp-attention LoRA config), not a
  dataclass field; direct attribute access would raise.
- DeepSeekV4(Indexer)Pool.get_index_k_scale_buffer signature fixed to the
  gather-based accessor API. At the pin this method was dead code whose call
  into dsa/index_buf_accessor.GetKAndS no longer matched the accessor
  signature; no other DSV4 caller exists (verified on pin + node70 snapshot).
- Upstream's CPU unit test test/registered/unit/layers/
  test_dsv4_nonpaged_indexer.py not included (asserts upstream defaults /
  v0.5.15-only constructs); its eligibility matrix is preserved in code.
- environ insertions placed after SGLANG_TOPK_TRANSFORM_512_TORCH; this was
  verified order-independent from the compress-state bf16 backport that was
  later removed after upstream absorbed that capability.

Gate-off residual (be precise): with the env OFF, two things change on the
paged path: (a) each forward_c4_indexer call now runs the cheap fail-closed
eligibility prelude (_get_nonpaged_indexer_plan's query-token threshold
compare, plus the env check in _can_use_nonpaged_indexer if the threshold
passes) before falling through to the paged path; (b) the paged
token_to_kv_pool.get_index_k_with_scale_buffer() fetch (which can block in
wait_layer_transfer()) moves from the prepare functions to immediately
before the paged mqa-logits call — a scheduling-order change mirroring
upstream. No numerical difference found by static reasoning (CPU-only
review; not GPU-verified), but not "execution-identical".

Env gates: SGLANG_OPT_DSV4_NONPAGED_INDEXER=0 (default) / 1 (opt-in);
SGLANG_OPT_DSV4_NONPAGED_INDEXER_MIN_QUERY_TOKENS=8192.

